---
import TorrentMock from './mocks/TorrentMock.astro'
---

  <section class="feat rev" id="torrents">
    <div class="wrap feat-in">
      <div class="feat-copy" data-reveal>
        <h2>Watch it while it is still downloading</h2>
        <p class="lede">
          Paste a magnet or open a <span class="mono">.torrent</span> and Frame Player starts playing while it downloads. Pieces near the playhead come first, and the seekbar shows what has arrived, so you know whether a jump will land.
        </p>
        <ul class="checks">
          <li><svg class="ic" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-check"/></svg>
            <span><b>Nothing downloads until you open it</b>, and seeding is off by default.</span></li>
          <li><svg class="ic" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-check"/></svg>
            <span><b>Subtitles inside the release attach themselves</b>, and the next episode is fetched ahead.</span></li>
          <li><svg class="ic" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-check"/></svg>
            <span><b>A stall says why:</b> download rate, peers and how much of the file is on disk.</span></li>
        </ul>
        <a class="more-link" href="/torrent-streaming">How torrent streaming works</a>
      </div>
      <div class="feat-mock" data-reveal style="--dl:1">
        <TorrentMock />
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
